  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1968-p27.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Pairing gives \\(S_n=-\\frac{n}{2}\\) for even \\(n\\) and \\(S_n=\\frac{n+1}{2}\\) for odd \\(n.\\) Hence \\(S_{17}=9,\\) \\(S_{33}=17,\\) \\(S_{50}=-25,\\) and their sum is \\(1.\\)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is B.",
      "hints": [
        "Pair terms as \\((1-2)+(3-4)+\\cdots\\)",
        "For even \\(n,\\) \\(S_n=-\\frac{n}{2};\\) for odd \\(n,\\) \\(S_n=\\frac{n+1}{2}\\)"
      ],
